+# A Flight 77 report in the Commission's watch-officer packet
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern. TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06. A Commission archive packet preserves a September 11 entry headed **09:45** that relays a DOJ account and includes **0933** in its text. A separate Commission request names DOJ and establishes what teleconference material staff sought in September 2003. The cited DOJ Command Center log and actual call-leg records remain unacquired. [National Archives finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf) · [Exact archive objects and locators](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Three uses of the time label
+
+| Source | Observation | Limit |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **Team 8 Box 17 packet, p. 3**, layout lines 1–8 | Date **09/11/2001**, Log Time **09:45**, marking **UNCLASSIFIED**, and **ICF** in the entry. The body begins a relay with **“DOJ CALLED TO SAY AT 0933”** and reports a call from Flight 77. The next line gives **“CELL PHONE”**. | The printed log time and reported time are different fields. The entry does not identify the system that originated the reported time, establish which leg it describes, or authenticate the reported device. |
+| **Same packet, p. 2**, layout lines 36–37 | A separate entry has **09:33** in its Log Time field. | Preserve this as a separate field occurrence. A matching number alone supplies no join to the p. 3 narrative or the cited DOJ log. |
+| **Commission staff report, note 268**, physical p. 95 | Staff attribute a **9:33** entry about an incoming report and a request for someone to go to an office to the DOJ Command Center Watch Officer Log, **0001–2400 HRS, September 11, 2001**. | This identifies a specific source and an action described by staff. The Team 8 packet's **09:45** entry attributes information to DOJ. Its reviewed fields do not authenticate it as the cited DOJ original. |
+
+[Commission archive ZIP, Team 8 Box 17 member named in the pins](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip) · [Commission staff report, note 268](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/staff-report-sept2005.pdf#page=95)
+
+The Team 8 entry's **CELL PHONE** description sits beside the earlier Airphone Usage analysis and the later DOJ briefing's airphone account. Keep the reports separate. This is evidence of how the receiving log described a relay at the time it records. Device type, caller attribution, calibrated time and linkage to any carrier row remain open. The DOJ-attributed relay and the staff note may rely on the same underlying communication. Their shared time does not provide independent corroboration of a call or an event-time measurement. [Earlier report and court-label comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5031c6dfa73e1f59491f259e00f168c37cb21788/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-usage-report-2026-10-27/README.md)
+
+## What Team 7 requested
+
+The Team 7 Box 20 cover is dated **September 3, 2003**. Its subject concerns **9/11 teleconferences**. It requests that agencies including DOJ provide responsive transcripts or other documents by **September 17, 2003** and defines its morning window as **08:30 to 12:00 EDT on September 11, 2001**. The subject, deadline and time window help identify the production or search records. The cover's scope concerns audio or video conferences. It does not name the full-day DOJ Watch Officer Log as an enclosure. The packet includes additional materials and fax pages. The screened packet yielded no authenticated join to the exact log cited in note 268. [Commission finding aid, Team 7 Box 20, p. 109](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf#page=109) · [Archive ZIP member, p. 1](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip)
+
+## Verification and next records
+
+Both exact mirror ZIP members were validated by byte range, size, CRC and SHA-256. The **33 physical pages** were screened using their text layers. Selected non-personal header, time, source and scope fields were checked in cropped renders. Neither PDF contains embedded files. This was a field and provenance comparison. No carrier record, original call or calibrated clock was tested.
+
+- **TEL04.** Obtain the full-day DOJ Command Center Watch Officer Log, the original record behind the Team 8 entry and any bridge, watch-transfer or receiving office evidence. Compare the surrounding entries, clock labels and same-leg identifiers before joining **09:33**, **0933** and **09:45** to an event. The participant and carrier records must support a device or route conclusion.
+- **TEL01–TEL02.** Seek the response to the September 3 teleconference request and itemized receipt or on-site review record, with the actual transcript, log or attachments. This request remains separate from Request 14, the usage-report production and the zero-duration exhibit's source mapping. [DOJ Commission production schedules and the prior search](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0deff1f3f7ad30466ba0b0375399c061cc253c19cc/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-doj-watchlog-record-series-2026-11-06/README.md)
